      "q": "4. I enjoy telling a story or arguing, I use my ____________ intelligence.",
      "a": "verbal\nMatch the job on the left with its description on the right.\n1. (i) Navigator - (a) Advises people what to do about jobs, personal problems, etc.\n(ii) Architect - (b) Works in politics, usually by standing for election.\n(iii) Politician - (c) Finds and monitors the route to get to a place, or the direction of travel.\n(iv) Engineer - (d) Reports on recent news for newspaper, radio, or TV.\n(v) Computer programmer - (e) Plans the design of a building, town, or city.\n(vi) Athlete - (f) Controls and puts together a programme of music.\n(vii) Disc jockey - (g) Works in sports or activities such as running, jumping etc.\n(viii) Composer - (h) Designs and builds things like roads, bridges, or engines.\n(ix) Counsellor - (i) Makes up notes to create music.\n(x) Journalist - (j) Designs the system by which a computer runs or gives information.\nAns:\n(i) Navigator - (c) Finds and monitors the route to get to a place, or the direction of travel.\n(ii) Architect - (e) Plans the design of a building, town, or city.\n(iii) Politician - (b) Works in politics, usually by standing for election.\n(iv) Engineer - (h) Designs and builds things like roads, bridges, or engines.\n(v) Computer Programmer - (j) Designs the system by which a computer runs or gives information.\n(vi) Athlete - (g) Works in sports or activities such as running, jumping etc.\n(vii) Disc jockey - (f) Controls and puts together a programme of music.\n(viii) Composer - (i) Makes up notes to create music.\n(ix) Counsellor - (a) Advises people what to do about jobs, personal problems, etc.\n(x) Journalist - (d) Reports on recent news for newspaper, radio, or TV.\nWRITING\nWrite a paragraph about yourself so that people who read it will get to know you better. You could write about yourself from any point of view, or choose one of the following topics.\nWhat I enjoy doing most\nWhat makes me angry\nWhat I hate to do\nWhat I want to become\n(Remember to give a reason or details of what you write about, so that anyone reading it will understand you better.)\nAfter you have finished your paragraph affix your photo on the sheet and display it on the wall. Read each other\u2019s paragraphs. Did you understand someone else better after you had read what\nhe/she wrote?\nI enjoy spending time outdoors, especially hiking in the mountains. The feeling of being surrounded by nature's beauty and the challenge of reaching a summit energises me. It's where I feel most alive and connected to the world around me. What makes me angry is injustice or when people are treated unfairly. I believe everyone deserves to be treated with respect and kindness. One thing I dislike doing is cleaning, especially washing dishes! I find it tedious and would rather spend that time doing something more engaging. In the future, I aspire to become a wildlife biologist. I've always been fascinated by animals and their habitats, and I want to contribute to conservation efforts to protect our planet's biodiversity.\nBy sharing these details, I hope others can understand my passions, values, and aspirations better.\nBenefits of NCERT Class 6 English Chapter 6 PDF Question Answer\nWho I Am Class 6 Questions And Answers provide a thorough explanation of the chapter, helping students grasp the content effectively.\nThey offer clear and concise answers to questions, making complex concepts easier to understand.\nBy engaging with Class 6th English Chapter 6 Question Answer, students enhance their reading, writing, and comprehension skills in English.\nThe solutions encourage critical thinking by analysing themes, characters, and events in the chapter.\nStudents can use Question Answers for self-assessment, checking their understanding, and identifying areas that need more focus mentioned in Class 6 English Chapter 6 PDF.\nNCERT Solutions promotes active learning as students actively engage with the text and its interpretations.\nBy exploring Who I Am Question Answer in depth, students develop an appreciation for literature and its various elements.\nClass 6 English Chapter 6 Question Answer collectively helps students not only understand the chapter but also to excel in their English studies by improving their overall language skills and analytical abilities.\nConclusion\nVedantu\u2019s NCERT Solutions for English Chapter 6 Who I Am Class 6 offers guidance for students exploring personal identity and self-expression. It\u2019s important to focus on understanding the themes of self-discovery and individuality presented in the chapter. By utilising Who I Am Class 6 Questions And Answers, students can gain clarity on the narratives and themes discussed, enhancing their comprehension skills and preparing effectively for exams. Class 6 English Lesson 6 Question Answer is essential for fostering a deeper appreciation of personal growth and identity exploration at the elementary level.\nChapter-wise Links for NCERT Solutions of English Class 6 (Honeysuckle)\nChapter-wise List NCERT Solutions Class 6 English (Prose)\nChapter 1 - Who Did Patrick's Homework\nChapter 2 - How the Dog Found Himself a New Master\nChapter 3 - Taro's Reward\nChapter 4 - An Indian American Woman in Space: Kalpana Chawla\nChapter 5 - A Different Kind of School\nChapter 7 - Fair Play\nChapter 8 - The Banyan Tree\nChapter-wise List NCERT Solutions Class 6 English (Poem)\nChapter 1 - A House, A Home\nChapter 2 - The Kite\nChapter 3 - The Quarrel\nChapter 4 - Beauty\nChapter 5 - Where Do All the Teachers Go?\nChapter 6 - The Wonderful Words\nChapter 7 - Vocation\nRelated Study Material for Class 6 English\nRelated Links to Study Material for Class 6 English\nCBSE Class 6 English Important Questions\nCBSE Class 6 English Grammar"
